#* {{quote-book|en|author=John Wentworth|title=A Complete System of Pleading: Comprehending the Most Approved Precedents and Forms of Practice; Consisting of Such as have Never before been Published: With an Index to the Principal Work, Incorporating and Making it a Continuation of Townshend's and Cornwall's Tables, to the Present Time; as Well as an Index of Reference to All the Ancient and Modern Entries Extant|location=London|publisher=Printed for G. G. and J. Robinson, [[w:Paternoster Row|Paternoster-Row]]|year=1798|volume=VII (Debt. Detinue.)|page=625|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=gE40AAAAIAAJ&pg=PA625|oclc=3949438|passage=Plea, that R. and E. being [[seise|ſeiſed]] of lands, were [[disseise|diſſeiſed]] by plaintiff, who [[demise#Verb|demiſed]] to defendent;{{sic}} R. and E. re-entered before any rent was '''unpaid'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Maclean v. Dunn and Watkins|journal=The Law Journal for the Year 1828: Comprising Reports of Cases in the Courts of Chancery, King's Bench, and Common Pleas, from Michaelmas Term 1827, to Trinity Term 1828, both inclusive. And Cases Connected with the Duties and Office of Magistrates, Decided during Those Terms|location=London|publisher=Printed by James Holmes, 4, Took's Court, {{w|Chancery Lane}}, for J. W. Paget, 5, Quality Court, Chancery Lane|date=19 May 1828|volume=IV|page=185, column 1|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=NncDAAAAQAAJ&pg=RA2-PA185|oclc=222561563|passage=[T]he plaintiff re-sold the said one hundred and sixty-five bags of Russian and German wool so remaining unaccepted by the defendants and '''unpaid''' for by them, by public sale, at and for a much less sum, to wit, the sum of 2000''l.'' less than the sum so agreed to be paid by the defendants for the same; {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Joel Waldfogel|chapter=Digital Piracy: Empirics|editors=Martin Peitz and Joel Waldfogel|title=The Oxford Handbook of the Digital Economy|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|Oxford University Press}}|year=2012|page=540|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=GFm-5WuYfYAC&pg=PA540|isbn=978-0-19-539784-0|passage=The volume of '''unpaid''' consumption in movies appears to be lower, particularly in the United States. Rob and Waldfogel (2007) report that only about 5 percent of movie consumption among University of Pennsylvania students in 2005 was '''unpaid''' (at a time when about half of a similar population's music consumption was '''unpaid''').}}
#: {{ant|en|paid}}
# Of work: done without [[agreed]] [[payment]], usually [[voluntarily]].
#: {{ux|en|an '''unpaid''' position}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Hisham S. El-Osta|author2=Mary C. Ahearn|chapter=Introduction|title=Estimating the Opportunity Cost of Unpaid Farm Labor for U.S. Farm Operators|series=Technical Bulletin|seriesvolume=no. 1848|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher={{w|Economic Research Service}}, {{w|United States Department of Agriculture}}|month=March|year=1996|page=1|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ucJDAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA1|oclc=37447588|passage=Farm labor is a critical input in agricultural production. Farm operators provide just about half of all labor hours in agriculture, most of which are '''unpaid'''. An additional 18 percent of farm labor hours are '''unpaid''' hours provided by farm household members, partners, and others.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific|Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific]], {{w|United Nations Development Programme}}|chapter=Introduction|title=Integrating Unpaid Work into National Policies|series=sales no. E.03.II.F.14|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|United Nations}}|year=2003|pages=7–8|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-uUtRRL8biAC&pg=PA|isbn=978-92-1-120151-2|passage=[A]ll people who perform work, paid or '''unpaid''', are economically active. It is, and always has been, quite misleading to regard people who perform only '''unpaid''' household work outside the SNA &#91;{{w|United Nations System of National Accounts}}&#93; production boundary as economically inactive.}}
#: {{syn|en|unsalaried|unwaged}}
